@startuml seq-kws-verification
' ============================================================
' Sequence Diagram: KWS Parent Verification (ADR-018, D1)
' Three legs with THREE DIFFERENT trust properties. The whole
' point of this diagram is that they are not interchangeable:
'   - SEND      us -> KWS. OAuth2 client-credentials over HTTP
'               Basic against a Keycloak realm. Outbound only.
'   - REDIRECT  parent's browser -> us. HMAC over
'               "status:external_payload", which carries NO
'               timestamp and NO nonce, so it is replayable BY
'               CONSTRUCTION. Therefore DISPLAY-ONLY.
'   - WEBHOOK   KWS -> us. Stripe-style t=/v1= over the RAW
'               body with a bounded clock skew. The ONLY leg
'               that writes consent state.
'
' Source files:
'   src/cyo_adventure/consent/service.py       (start_parent_verification,
'                                                record_parent_verified)
'   src/cyo_adventure/consent/kws_client.py     (token mint + send-email;
'                                                _TOKEN_PATH is a Keycloak
'                                                realm, _SEND_EMAIL_PATH is
'                                                the service API: two DISTINCT
'                                                hosts)
'   src/cyo_adventure/consent/external_payload.py (mint/serialize/parse the
'                                                correlation; 250-char cap
'                                                enforced before the request
'                                                is built)
'   src/cyo_adventure/api/kws_webhook.py        (POST /api/v1/webhooks/kws/
'                                                parent-verified)
'   src/cyo_adventure/api/kws_redirect.py       (GET /api/v1/consent/kws/return)
'   src/cyo_adventure/core/config.py            (kws_* settings, the
'                                                all-or-none credential
'                                                validator, and the
'                                                declared-methods validator)
'   src/cyo_adventure/db/models.py              (KwsVerification)
'   supabase/migrations/20260809130000_add_kws_verification.sql
'   docs/planning/adr/adr-018-childrens-privacy-compliance.md (D1)
' ============================================================

skinparam defaultFontName "Roboto"
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Parent / Guardian" as parent
participant "Guardian console\n(frontend)" as console
participant "consent/service.py\nstart_parent_verification" as service
database "kws_verification\n(id IS the correlation,\nenabled_methods snapshot)" as db
participant "consent/kws_client.py\nOAuth2 client-credentials" as client
participant "KWS auth realm\nauth.kidswebservices.com\n(Keycloak)" as kws_auth
participant "KWS service API\n/v1/verifications/send-email" as kws_api

' ========== Leg 1: SEND ==========
note over parent,kws_api: SEND (us -> KWS) - the row is committed BEFORE the email is requested

parent -> console : "start parent verification"
console -> service : "start_parent_verification(user_id, email)"
service -> service : "correlation = mint_correlation()\n(the row id IS the correlation;\nno DB default, caller supplies it)"
service -> db : "INSERT kws_verification\n(status='sent', requested_at,\n kws_environment,\n enabled_methods=list(settings...))"
note right of db
  **#CRITICAL data integrity.** This INSERT is
  COMMITTED, on its OWN session, BEFORE the
  outbound call. Sending first can put a real
  email in front of a real parent with no row
  for the webhook to match, and KWS will not
  replay a delivery on request, so that attempt
  is unattributable FOREVER.
  Merely flushing into the caller's unit of work
  reintroduces the hole by a longer route: the
  very error the ordering exists to survive
  rolls the row back.
  The reverse failure (a ``sent`` row for an
  email that never went) is cheap and self-heals.
end note
db --> service : "committed"
service -> client : "send_verification_email(\n  parent_email, externalPayload=id)"
client -> kws_auth : "POST /auth/realms/kws/protocol/\nopenid-connect/token\n[HTTP Basic: client_id + api_key]"
kws_auth --> client : "access_token (bounded lifetime)"
client -> kws_api : "POST /v1/verifications/send-email\n{parentEmail, externalPayload}\n[Bearer; User-Agent REQUIRED]"
note right of client
  Vendor constraints, learned empirically:
  * a missing ``User-Agent`` is a 403
    "Request blocked", not a 400
  * rate limit is **10 requests/hour per unique
    parent email**, in Test and production alike
  * ``externalPayload`` caps at 250 chars
end note
kws_api --> client : "202 accepted"
client --> service : "ok"
service --> console : "VerificationCorrelation(attempt_id)"
kws_api -> parent : "verification email"

' ========== Leg 2: REDIRECT (display only) ==========
note over parent,kws_api: REDIRECT return (parent's browser -> us) - DISPLAY ONLY, writes NOTHING

participant "api/kws_redirect.py\nGET /api/v1/consent/kws/return" as redirect

parent -> kws_api : "completes Epic's hosted flow\n(card check, or AgeGraph hit)"
kws_api -> parent : "302 to our return URL\n?status=..&externalPayload=..&signature=.."
parent -> redirect : "GET /api/v1/consent/kws/return"
redirect -> redirect : "HMAC(KWS_VERIFICATION_SECRET,\n f\"{status}:{external_payload}\")\ncompare_digest"
alt "secret unset"
  redirect -> parent : "400 ConfigurationError\n(refuses to render a result from\nan unverifiable redirect)"
else "signature absent or wrong"
  redirect -> parent : "400 'We could not confirm this link'\n(same page for wrong key, wrong\nsignature, and missing signature)"
else "signature valid"
  redirect -> parent : "200 result page\n(Cache-Control: no-store)"
end
note over redirect
  **Why this leg may never write consent state.**
  The signed message carries no timestamp and no
  nonce, so a URL a parent once received replays
  forever. A consent record creatable by replaying
  an old link would not be a consent record.
  This route therefore renders and returns; the
  webhook below is what makes it true.
end note

' ========== Leg 3: WEBHOOK (the only writer) ==========
note over parent,kws_api: WEBHOOK (KWS -> us) - the ONLY leg that writes consent state

participant "api/kws_webhook.py\nPOST /api/v1/webhooks/kws/\nparent-verified" as webhook
participant "consent/service.py\nrecord_parent_verified" as resolve

kws_api -> webhook : "POST parent-verified\n{orgId, productId, externalPayload, ...}\n[t=..,v1=.. over the RAW body]"
webhook -> webhook : "HMAC(KWS_WEBHOOK_SECRET, raw body)\n+ bounded clock skew\n(KWS_WEBHOOK_MAX_SKEW_SECONDS)"
alt "secret unset, or signature/skew fails"
  webhook --> kws_api : "400 ConfigurationError\nor 401 AuthenticationError\n(unset does NOT mean trust unsigned)"
else "signature valid"
  webhook -> webhook : "_is_for_us(): orgId matches, and\nproductId matches OR is not yet pinned\n(vacuously true until a first delivery\nreveals the id)"
  webhook -> resolve : "record_parent_verified(outcome)"
  resolve -> db : "SELECT ... FOR UPDATE\nby attempt_id, then set\nstatus='verified'|'failed',\nresolved_at, transaction_id"
  db --> resolve : "resolved"
  resolve --> webhook : "ok"
  webhook --> kws_api : "200"
end

note over webhook,db
  **The callback does not report WHICH method ran**
  (ADR-018 D1). Combined with the AgeGraph branch,
  which verifies a parent by inheritance from another
  KWS-enabled service, we cannot evidence HOW a given
  parent was verified. That is why the row stores
  ``enabled_methods`` as a snapshot taken at SEND time
  rather than a live read: the operator's own versioned
  configuration is the compliance evidence, and it must
  not mutate under a past verification.
end note

legend bottom
  Three legs, three trust properties (ADR-018 D1):
  |= Leg |= Direction |= Authenticated by |= Replayable? |= May write consent state |
  | Send | us -> KWS | OAuth2 client-credentials (HTTP Basic -> Bearer) | n/a (outbound) | creates the ``sent`` row, before the call |
  | Redirect return | parent's browser -> us | HMAC over "status:external_payload" | **YES, by construction** (no timestamp, no nonce) | **never** |
  | Webhook | KWS -> us | Stripe-style t=/v1= over the raw body, bounded skew | no (skew-bounded) | **yes, the only one** |
  ----
  Environment partition: every row stores its own ``kws_environment``. KWS reports nothing that
  would let it be re-derived later, and the app's guard against production credentials fires only
  when ENVIRONMENT == "local", which no deployed tier is. A Test verification is not a valid VPC.
endlegend

@enduml
